ry","decision_margin":-0.6062,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'A present scc run over a file above the configured LOC threshold emits a normalized metric match for that file.'","Plan: 'Add a physically withheld RED oracle that observes a real or argv-faithful scc boundary' — substrate for the *permanent* positive test is left unspecified.","A mock that emits Files[] independent of argv would satisfy AC1 without --by-file ever being sent (VERIFY-COMMAND taxonomy item 4: fixture does not exercise the claim)."],"finding":"The positive-match acceptance criterion (AC1) does not state whether its permanent test observes a real scc binary or a mock. If the permanent positive-match test uses a mock that returns populated Files entries regardless of argv, it would pass even against the pre-fix command (which omits --by-file), so the positive test alone does not prove the defect is fixed. The argv-sensitive test (AC3) is what actually anchors the fix; the plan should make explicit that the argv assertion and the match assertion are distinct and that the positive path either runs against a real/argv-faithful boundary or is paired with the argv check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f385bb679b2024f22","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1 / Plan bullet 'Add positive match ... coverage'","norm_id":"n7ff676a0dcc8f100","priority":0.3438,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Specify in the plan that the positive-match test either invokes a real scc binary over the >800-LOC fixture, or asserts on an argv-faithful fake that only returns per-file entries when --by-file is present.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"ye